In this project, I worked with pointers and dynamic memory allocation using C++.
* Implemented swapping of two variables using pointers.
* Used pointer variables to access and modify memory values.
* Displayed values before and after the swap operation.
* Created a dynamic array using memory allocation at runtime.
* Accepted user input and stored values in the dynamically allocated array.
* Displayed the stored array elements using pointer-based memory management.
* Practiced object creation and object access through pointers.
* Used class methods to organize and execute different operations.
This project helped me understand pointers, memory addresses, dynamic memory allocation, object pointers, and basic memory management concepts in C++.
